# Cursor-native subagent orchestration (L9)

When two or more bounded actions are independently ready:

1. Keep architecture, synthesis, integration, and user decisions with the main agent.
2. Use existing autonomy readiness, lease, and resource-claim contracts.
3. Launch all currently ready non-conflicting Cursor subagents in one batch.
4. Continue independent critical-path work while background subagents run.
5. Require one `l9.cursor-subagent.result.v1` document from each subagent.
6. Reject narrative-only completion.
7. Require a different agent for verifier/reviewer work.
8. Submit only accepted documents through the cursor-subagents result bridge.
9. Do not poll CI, discover PR work, select models, or launch external agents.
